# One line-ending policy on every platform: stored as LF, checked out as LF.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone rewrites every file the moment git touches it (rewriting the panel, the
# backend and the docs into CRLF while the warning scrolls past), and every later diff is noise. The
# gates are line-ending agnostic — the canary run re-writes and re-reads the real files byte for byte
# within a single run — so a single policy is strictly better than two.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Measured evidence, never normalised.
*.png binary
